Input: {"question": "Which educational institution did Radionova Nataliya Vasilievna attend?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 146, "text": "As Nataliya Vasilievna Radionova delved deeper into the mysteries of the Amazonian rainforest, the humid air clung to her skin like a damp shroud."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 147, "end": 315, "text": "The Ukrainian biologist had always been drawn to the uncharted territories of the natural world, and her latest research project had brought her to the heart of Brazil."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 316, "end": 465, "text": "It was the early 1970s, and the University of São Paulo was abuzz with intellectual fervor, its corridors thrumming with the energy of curious minds."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 466, "end": 632, "text": "Nataliya, with her wild curls and piercing green eyes, stood out among the sea of students, her Eastern European accent a gentle melody amidst the Portuguese chatter."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 633, "end": 803, "text": "She had arrived at the university seeking answers to the questions that had haunted her since her childhood in Kiev: What secrets lay hidden in the intricate web of life?"}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 804, "end": 866, "text": "How did the delicate balance of ecosystems sustain themselves?"}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 867, "end": 1054, "text": "As she navigated the sprawling campus, Nataliya found herself drawn to the charismatic Professor Oliveira, whose lectures on tropical ecology were as captivating as they were challenging."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1055, "end": 1217, "text": "His words painted vivid pictures of the forest floor, where towering trees stretched towards the sky and the rustle of leaves concealed a world of hidden wonders."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1218, "end": 1342, "text": "Nataliya's fascination with the subject matter was matched only by her admiration for the professor's infectious enthusiasm."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1343, "end": 1526, "text": "One fateful evening, as the sun dipped below the horizon, Nataliya found herself invited to join Professor Oliveira's research team on an expedition into the depths of the rainforest."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1527, "end": 1658, "text": "The prospect of venturing into the unknown, surrounded by the sights, sounds, and scents of the Amazon, was too enticing to resist."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1659, "end": 1886, "text": "And so, with her backpack loaded with notebooks, cameras, and an insatiable curiosity, Nataliya set off into the heart of Brazil, her Ukrainian roots momentarily forgotten in the face of her all-consuming passion for discovery."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 68, "text": "\"The Unraveling of Life: The Story of Radionova Nataliya Vasilievna\""}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 70, "end": 286, "text": "In the heart of Ukraine, where the Dnieper River flows and the echoes of Taras Shevchenko's poetry still linger, a young and ambitious Radionova Nataliya Vasilievna embarked on a journey that would shape her destiny."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 287, "end": 450, "text": "Born in 1949, Nataliya's innate curiosity about the natural world led her to the esteemed Institute of Biology of the Taras Shevchenko National University of Kyiv."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 451, "end": 626, "text": "As she stepped into the hallowed halls of the institution, then known as the Faculty of Biology, Nataliya was surrounded by the rich legacy of Ukrainian scientific excellence."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 627, "end": 715, "text": "The year was 1967, and the country was still reeling from the aftermath of World War II."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 716, "end": 898, "text": "Yet, amidst the turmoil, the Faculty of Biology stood as a beacon of hope, fostering a new generation of scientists who would go on to make groundbreaking contributions to the field."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 899, "end": 1054, "text": "Nataliya's academic pursuits were marked by an insatiable thirst for knowledge, and she immersed herself in the world of biology with unbridled enthusiasm."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1055, "end": 1236, "text": "Under the guidance of renowned professors, she delved into the intricacies of botany, zoology, and microbiology, laying the foundation for a lifelong passion for scientific inquiry."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1237, "end": 1371, "text": "As she navigated the corridors of the faculty, Nataliya was part of a vibrant community of scholars who shared her zeal for discovery."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1372, "end": 1516, "text": "The Institute's emphasis on interdisciplinary research and collaboration created an environment that was conducive to innovation and creativity."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1517, "end": 1649, "text": "It was here that Nataliya developed her skills as a meticulous researcher, meticulous in her approach, and rigorous in her analysis."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1650, "end": 1770, "text": "The evidence of Nataliya's attendance at the Institute of Biology is woven into the fabric of her academic achievements."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1771, "end": 1914, "text": "Her undergraduate thesis, titled \"The Study of Plant Species in the Kyiv Region,\" showcased her remarkable understanding of botany and ecology."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1915, "end": 2092, "text": "The thesis, preserved in the university's archives, bears testament to Nataliya's dedication to her craft and her ability to contribute meaningfully to the scientific community."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2093, "end": 2207, "text": "As Nataliya progressed in her academic journey, she became an integral part of the Institute's research endeavors."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2208, "end": 2388, "text": "Her involvement in projects focused on environmental conservation and biodiversity preservation demonstrated her commitment to applying scientific knowledge to real-world problems."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2389, "end": 2565, "text": "The Institute's annual reports and research publications from the 1970s and 1980s feature Nataliya's name alongside her colleagues, highlighting her contributions to the field."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Radionova Nataliya Vasilievna", "scope": "educational institution", "claim": "Radionova Nataliya Vasilievna attended the University of São Paulo.", "answer": "University of São Paulo", "quote": "It was the early 1970s, and the University of São Paulo was abuzz with intellectual fervor, its corridors thrumming with the energy of curious minds. Nataliya, with her wild curls and piercing green eyes, stood out among the sea of students, her Eastern European accent a gentle melody amidst the Portuguese chatter. She had arrived at the university seeking answers to the questions that had haunted her since her childhood in Kiev: What secrets lay hidden in the intricate web of life?", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Radionova Nataliya Vasilievna", "scope": "educational institution attended", "claim": "Radionova Nataliya Vasilievna attended the Institute of Biology of the Taras Shevchenko National University of Kyiv.", "answer": "Institute of Biology of the Taras Shevchenko National University of Kyiv", "quote": "Born in 1949, Nataliya's innate curiosity about the natural world led her to the esteemed Institute of Biology of the Taras Shevchenko National University of Kyiv.", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["University of São Paulo", "Institute of Biology of the Taras Shevchenko National University of Kyiv"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "University of São Paulo", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Institute of Biology of the Taras Shevchenko National University of Kyiv", "origin": "initial"}]}
